1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,680
This is a rooftop in Islamabad.

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:09,480
Every heat warning here is calculated at the airport, twenty-nine kilometres away.

3
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:14,100
So I built two, about fifteen dollars each.

4
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:21,720
The white shield matters. Bare, the sensor read forty-three degrees. Shielded, thirty-six.

5
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:24,440
One on the roof, over concrete.

6
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:29,960
This one at street level, on a shaded wall over asphalt.

7
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:36,120
Every five minutes, both report to a service on Nebius Token Factory.

8
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:42,680
The heat index is calculated with the NOAA formula, in code. Not a model.

9
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:49,080
There is a correct answer, and a model would give me a plausible one.

10
00:00:49,080 --> 00:00:54,240
NVIDIA Nemotron decides what a person should do.

11
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:57,520
Most readings stay with Nemotron Nano.

12
00:00:57,520 --> 00:01:04,440
When the danger is high enough that being wrong hurts somebody, it escalates to Nemotron Super.

13
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:10,960
That is decided on conditions, not on asking the model how sure it feels.

14
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:18,560
Now watch, when I cover the camera. It stops. It cannot see, so it will not advise.

15
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:20,640
I found this the hard way.

16
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:26,840
The vision model was looking at night photographs, almost black, and saying it could see.

17
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:30,280
Now brightness is checked first, in code.

18
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:38,080
The advice comes out in Urdu, because the people this is for do not read English dashboards.

19
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:41,280
Tavily checks the load-shedding schedule.

20
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:48,880
No power means no fan, and the fan is the only cooling most outdoor workers have.

21
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:55,800
Six days. At three in the morning, my sensors and the airport agree.

22
00:01:55,800 --> 00:02:01,640
By six in the evening, they read seven degrees warmer. Nearly four times in ten,

23
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:04,640
the airport would have given a lower risk band.

24
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:08,280
The airport is not wrong. It is just not describing this place.
